       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** the usual prescription ceiling is 3,200 mg/day, given as at most 800 mg per dose. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** this order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the maximum single dose. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
